          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>The sampling distribution of $\\bar{X}$ has standard error $\\sigma/\\sqrt{n} = 11.6/\\sqrt{32} = 11.6/5.6569 = 2.0506$. So $Z = \\dfrac{\\bar{x}-\\mu}{\\sigma/\\sqrt{n}} = \\dfrac{94.0 - 90.3}{2.0506} = \\dfrac{3.7}{2.0506} = 1.8043$. (Dividing by $\\sigma$ instead of the standard error would wrongly give $0.319$.)</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>Phân phối mẫu của $\\bar{X}$ có sai số chuẩn $\\sigma/\\sqrt{n} = 11.6/\\sqrt{32} = 11.6/5.6569 = 2.0506$. Vậy $Z = \\dfrac{\\bar{x}-\\mu}{\\sigma/\\sqrt{n}} = \\dfrac{94.0 - 90.3}{2.0506} = \\dfrac{3.7}{2.0506} = 1.8043$. (Nếu chia cho $\\sigma$ thay vì sai số chuẩn sẽ ra sai $0.319$.)</p></div>"
